      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the late 1850s, Arlington Heights’ truck farms were shipping dairy and vegetables to Chicago, feeding the city’s booming market.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arlington_Heights%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1927, Arlington Park racetrack was founded, turning the village into a regional destination for horse racing enthusiasts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arlington_Heights%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The original Arlington High School, built in 1922, closed in 1984 and now houses the private Christian Liberty Academy.",
